                <pb facs="0865" n="765" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg765"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">765.84/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Ethiopia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">George</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Addis
                                Ababa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-12-06T13:00:00+02:35">December 6, 1934—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 1:47 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Anglo-Ethiopian Boundary Commission came as far as Italian military post at
                    Wal Wal water hole, Ogaden Desert, November 23rd and was denied permission to
                    proceed behind its lines although far within Ethiopia. Italian reply to protest
                    was tank and airplane demonstration at Wal Wal yesterday. Commission has
                    returned to Addis Ababa but Ethiopian escort entrenched opposite Italian post
                    which has apparently been established there 3 years unknown to Ethiopian
                    Government. Situation regarded extremely grave here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
